@host = http://localhost:5100
@customerId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### Check out the basket filled in Basket.http - expect 202 Accepted + Location
### The reply names the order BEFORE it exists; the consumer creates it a moment later
POST {{host}}/api/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "{{customerId}}" }

### Check out an EMPTY basket (a fresh customer) - expect 422
POST {{host}}/api/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222" }

### One order - paste the id from the 202 Location
### Expect 404 until the consumer catches up (usually well under a second), then 200
GET {{host}}/api/orders/01a0a977-e689-754d-9a1f-f492fb99f7ab

### All orders for one customer - expect 200 OK
GET {{host}}/api/orders/customer/{{customerId}}

### Cancel the order - expect 204 No Content
POST {{host}}/api/orders/01a08b13-9871-77cd-91a5-fc0c8f36fa93/cancel

### Cancel it AGAIN - only a placed order can be cancelled; expect 422
POST {{host}}/api/orders/01a08b13-9871-77cd-91a5-fc0c8f36fa93/cancel

### The same order, ONCE: send this request TWICE with the same Idempotency-Key
### Both runs answer 202 with the SAME Location - one checkout, one order, no duplicate
POST {{host}}/api/checkout
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-key-0002

{ "customerId": "{{customerId}}" }
